From dc7e7928c8955f4ec9feff260d9742d5c461eb5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shandongtlb <40312509+shandongtlb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:50:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] sched/hmbird: restore stock cluster uclamp
 initialization write

Initialize uclamp_min alongside id during first cluster construction. The stock Image contains five 64-bit stores covering both u32 fields; the previous candidate wrote only id after the initial memset. The actual ARM64 object now reproduces all five stores, with no other .text changes.

Evidence: stock Image SHA256 0b4b3aadd775009d88f39d0738ee7fa1a8a053444f668c2a762d0ea31f86e6a5, stores at offsets 0x119d28, 0x119d4c, 0x119d70, 0x119d94, 0x119dbc. Preserve bool and out-of-range trap differences as separate audit limits; no config or layout changes.
---
 kernel/sched/hmbird/hmbird.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/hmbird/hmbird.c b/kernel/sched/hmbird/hmbird.c
index b54c94c8b..3b12eedb6 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/hmbird/hmbird.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/hmbird/hmbird.c
@@ -78,6 +78,7 @@ static void hmbird_build_clusters(void)
 		if (cpumask_empty(&hmbird_cluster[id].cpus))
 			break;
 		hmbird_cluster[id].id = id;
+		hmbird_cluster[id].uclamp_min = 0;
 		spin_lock_init(&hmbird_cluster[id].lock);
 		hmbird_nr_clusters++;
 	}
